{"authorDailyContributionsMap":{"preyjwal":[{"date":"2026-11-02T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"884ab5ba3fdabf66caedc63537db65a8df2e660a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Relax email local-part validation","messageBody":"The email validator rejects addresses that are valid under RFC 5322\nand that real mail systems issue, such as o\u0027connor@example.com,\nalice++sales@example.com and john__doe@example.com. Users with these\naddresses cannot save their contacts, and a saved file containing one\nis treated as corrupt when it is loaded.\n\nAllow the apostrophe and the other special characters RFC 5322\npermits in the local part, and let them repeat and appear at its\nstart or end. A period keeps the dot-atom rule: it may not start or\nend the local part or appear two or more times in a row. The domain\nrules are unchanged.\n\nThe slash stays disallowed because it is the command delimiter. With\n\"e/ a/b@example.com\", \"a/\" would be read as the address prefix and\nleave the email empty, so accepting it would turn a valid email into\na confusing error.\n\nThe constraint message and the User Guide are updated to match.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":9,"deletions":7},"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":55,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"653cbf80e6a2fd484000d892ba9f7f0f9cd9863e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject null entries in the data file when loading","messageBody":"A data file with a null entry, such as {\"persons\":[null]},\n{\"meetings\":[null]} or a null inside a person\u0027s \"tags\", crashes\nPingBook at startup with a NullPointerException. The UG says an\ninvalid data file makes PingBook start with an empty address book,\nand MainApp already does this for a DataLoadingException, but an\nNPE escapes that handling.\n\nReport these entries as IllegalValueException, like every other\ninvalid value in the file, so they reach the existing handling.\nNull persons and meetings are rejected when the address book is\nconverted to the model, and null tags or tag names when a person is\nconverted. The person tag check matches the one JsonAdaptedMeeting\nalready has.\n\nNull entries are rejected rather than skipped, so a partly corrupt\nfile is never loaded with some of its data silently missing.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":11,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":52,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"48a88bf8dea57f54a67913bc56769f9e394c43a2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject JSON files that contain only null","messageBody":"A data or preferences file whose entire content is the JSON literal\nnull crashes PingBook at startup with a NullPointerException. Jackson\nreturns a null object for it, and JsonUtil.readJsonFile then wraps\nthat in Optional.of(). The NPE is not a DataLoadingException, so the\nfallbacks in MainApp never run, and the UG\u0027s promise to start with an\nempty address book or default preferences is broken.\n\nTreat a null result as an unreadable file, like any other malformed\nJSON, so readJsonFile throws DataLoadingException. This is done in\nthe shared reader, so both addressbook.json and preferences.json are\ncovered.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":3,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":20,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"5ae87dc1aa88efdf6461a40660c6695e292eaa62","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge upstream/master into relax-email-validation","messageBody":"Resolve the User Guide conflict by taking master\u0027s reformatted Field\nformats table and re-applying the relaxed Email row to it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"5d1be9df24c1eb8e3c25fbff8a0c2ea7bd3d0010","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #216 from preyjwal/relax-email-validation","messageBody":"Relax email local-part validation","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"7e8519d6ba2d3cdf6ae44e8b20772a97256b3e51","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject meetings with end time not after start in storage","messageBody":"A meeting file with endTime at or before startTime loads without\ncomplaint, because the time range is only validated by the add and\nedit parsers. Editing any other field of such a meeting afterwards\nfails with \"Invalid time range\", even though the user never touched\nthe times.\n\nValidate the time range when converting stored meetings to the model,\nas is already done for the other fields, so a bad range is reported at\nload time instead of surfacing later in an unrelated command.\n\nAs with other invalid stored values, a data file that fails this check\nis not loaded and the app starts with empty data.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":4,"deletions":0},"test-code":{"insertions":27,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"097492dc13f5ffac149daf4110e0eb64be7db19e","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027master\u0027 into fix-null-entries-in-data-file","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"e0e83a0aef8d5638ff932e0d39e528c7feee77a7","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #219 from preyjwal/fix-null-entries-in-data-file","messageBody":"Fix App crashing at startup on a data file with a null entries","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]}],"kaih4n":[{"date":"2026-10-31T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"92ddeeb05ebfdf599a093e13d6325add3e62a568","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix findm validation","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":8,"deletions":1}}}]},{"date":"2026-11-02T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"9dffbe8fa3855146613b9d1fce30bff08c65f4b6","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update Name.java","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":2,"deletions":3},"test-code":{"insertions":4,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"d785048265b217bafdea3f5ecab9e3d59c036fa5","isMergeCommit":false,"mess